TASK 1 — Shell Scripting: Service Status Report  (15 pts, ~10 min)
Skriptiranje ljuske: izvještaj o stanju usluga
----------------------------------------------------------
The team lead wants a quick script that reports the live status of a list of
system services, so it can be run on demand without remembering each
systemctl invocation by hand.
Voditelj tima želi brzu skriptu koja izvještava o trenutnom stanju popisa
sistemskih usluga, kako bi se mogla pokrenuti po potrebi bez pamćenja
svake systemctl naredbe napamet.

1. Create an executable script at /home/student/bin/{{ rh134_script_name }}.  (3 pts)
   Stvorite izvršnu skriptu na /home/student/bin/{{ rh134_script_name }}.

2. The script must loop over these service names: {{ exam_service_list }}.  (4 pts)
   Skripta mora prolaziti kroz sljedeće nazive usluga: {{ exam_service_list }}.

3. For each service, print one line in the exact format:  (5 pts)
     SERVICE: <name> ACTIVE: <active|inactive> ENABLED: <enabled|disabled>
   using the live output of systemctl is-active and systemctl is-enabled.
   Za svaku uslugu ispišite jedan redak u točnom formatu:
     SERVICE: <naziv> ACTIVE: <active|inactive> ENABLED: <enabled|disabled>
   koristeći trenutni izlaz naredbi systemctl is-active i systemctl is-enabled.

4. Running the script must (over)write its output to {{ rh134_report_file }} —
   running it twice must not duplicate lines.  (3 pts)
   Pokretanje skripte mora (pre)pisati izlaz u {{ rh134_report_file }} —
   dvostruko pokretanje ne smije udvostručiti retke.

Tip / Savjet: use command substitution ($(...)) to capture the output of
systemctl is-active / is-enabled into variables before formatting the line.
Koristite supstituciju naredbi ($(...)) za hvatanje izlaza naredbi
systemctl is-active / is-enabled u varijable prije formatiranja retka.


TASK 2 — LVM: Build, Mount, and Extend Storage  (20 pts, ~20 min)
LVM: izgradnja, montiranje i proširenje pohrane
--------------------------------------------------------------
A new raw disk has been attached to your system (/dev/sdb, completely empty).
The team needs it turned into a persistently-mounted LVM volume — and then
the team realizes the initial size estimate was too small, so it must be
grown without losing data.
Novi sirovi disk je priključen na vaš sustav (/dev/sdb, potpuno prazan).
Tim treba da se on pretvori u trajno montirani LVM volumen — a zatim tim
shvati da je početna procjena veličine bila premala, pa ga treba proširiti
bez gubitka podataka.

1. Partition /dev/sdb for LVM use (one partition, LVM flag set), then create
   a physical volume on it and a volume group named {{ rh134_vg_name }}.  (4 pts)
   Particionirajte /dev/sdb za LVM (jedna particija, postavljena LVM oznaka),
   zatim stvorite fizički volumen na njoj i grupu volumena pod nazivom
   {{ rh134_vg_name }}.

2. Create a logical volume named {{ rh134_lv_name }} of size
   {{ rh134_lv_initial_size }} in that volume group, format it XFS, and
   mount it persistently at {{ rh134_mount_point }} (must survive a reboot).  (7 pts)
   Stvorite logički volumen pod nazivom {{ rh134_lv_name }} veličine
   {{ rh134_lv_initial_size }} u toj grupi volumena, formatirajte ga kao XFS
   i trajno montirajte na {{ rh134_mount_point }} (mora preživjeti ponovno
   pokretanje).

3. Create a file at {{ rh134_mount_point }}/marker.txt containing the text
   "{{ exam_variant }} volume ready".  (2 pts)
   Stvorite datoteku na {{ rh134_mount_point }}/marker.txt sa sadržajem
   "{{ exam_variant }} volume ready".

4. Extend the logical volume by {{ rh134_lv_extend_size }} and grow the XFS
   filesystem to use the new space — without unmounting or losing the
   marker file.  (7 pts)
   Proširite logički volumen za {{ rh134_lv_extend_size }} i povećajte XFS
   datotečni sustav da iskoristi novi prostor — bez odmontiranja ili
   gubitka marker datoteke.

Tip / Savjet: "parted ... unit MiB print" shows sizes in a more LVM-friendly
unit than the default. After lvextend, the filesystem itself needs a
separate command to recognize the new space.
"parted ... unit MiB print" prikazuje veličine u jedinici prikladnijoj za
LVM. Nakon lvextend, datotečni sustav treba zasebnu naredbu da prepozna
novi prostor.


TASK 3 — Persistent Logging: journald + rsyslog Routing  (15 pts, ~12 min)
Trajno bilježenje: journald i rsyslog usmjeravanje
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
The operations team wants two logging improvements: journal entries must
survive reboots (currently they're volatile), and messages of a specific
severity from a specific subsystem must be routed to their own dedicated
file for faster triage.
Operativni tim želi dva poboljšanja u bilježenju: zapisi journala moraju
preživjeti ponovno pokretanje (trenutno su nestalni), a poruke određene
ozbiljnosti iz određenog podsustava moraju biti usmjerene u vlastitu
namjensku datoteku radi brže obrade.

1. Configure systemd-journald so that journal entries are stored
   persistently on disk (must survive a reboot).  (5 pts)
   Konfigurirajte systemd-journald tako da se zapisi journala trajno
   pohranjuju na disk (moraju preživjeti ponovno pokretanje).

2. Create an rsyslog configuration file that routes all messages matching
   facility {{ rh134_rsyslog_facility }} at priority {{ rh134_rsyslog_priority }}
   (and higher) to the file {{ rh134_log_file }}.  (6 pts)
   Stvorite rsyslog konfiguracijsku datoteku koja usmjerava sve poruke koje
   odgovaraju facility {{ rh134_rsyslog_facility }} na razini
   {{ rh134_rsyslog_priority }} (i više) u datoteku {{ rh134_log_file }}.

3. Generate a test message using logger with the matching facility and
   priority, and confirm it appears in {{ rh134_log_file }}.  (4 pts)
   Generirajte testnu poruku naredbom logger s odgovarajućim facility i
   priority, te potvrdite da se pojavljuje u {{ rh134_log_file }}.

Tip / Savjet: persistent journald storage requires a specific directory to
exist before the service is restarted — check the journalctl man page or
"man systemd-journald" for where that directory lives. Rsyslog routing
rules use the syntax "facility.priority    /path/to/file".
Trajna journald pohrana zahtijeva da određeni direktorij postoji prije
ponovnog pokretanja usluge — provjerite man stranicu journalctl ili
"man systemd-journald" gdje se taj direktorij nalazi. Rsyslog pravila
usmjeravanja koriste sintaksu "facility.priority    /putanja/do/datoteke".


TASK 4 — File Transfer: rsync Backup and Secure Upload  (15 pts, ~10 min)
Prijenos datoteka: rsync sigurnosna kopija i siguran prijenos
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Before any risky changes, the team always backs up configuration directories
and securely ships specific files off-box.
Prije bilo kakvih rizičnih promjena, tim uvijek izrađuje sigurnosne kopije
konfiguracijskih direktorija i sigurno šalje određene datoteke izvan sustava.

1. Use rsync in archive mode to copy the entire /etc/exam-source/ directory
   (provided on your system) to a new local directory
   /home/student/{{ rh134_backup_dir }}/, preserving permissions, ownership,
   and timestamps.  (6 pts)
   Naredbom rsync u arhivskom načinu kopirajte cijeli direktorij
   /etc/exam-source/ (dostupan na vašem sustavu) u novi lokalni direktorij
   /home/student/{{ rh134_backup_dir }}/, čuvajući dozvole, vlasništvo i
   vremenske oznake.

2. Securely copy the file
   /home/student/{{ rh134_backup_dir }}/exam-source/manifest.txt to the path
   /home/student/uploaded-{{ exam_variant }}.txt ON THE REPO VM (172.16.16.121),
   authenticating as the student user over SSH/SCP/SFTP.  (9 pts)
   Sigurno kopirajte datoteku
   /home/student/{{ rh134_backup_dir }}/exam-source/manifest.txt na putanju
   /home/student/uploaded-{{ exam_variant }}.txt NA REPO VM-u (172.16.16.121),
   autenticirajući se kao korisnik student preko SSH/SCP/SFTP.

NOTE / NAPOMENA: This is your first SSH connection to the repo VM — you will
see a host key prompt the first time. Accepting it is expected and safe.
Ovo je vaša prva SSH veza na repo VM — pri prvom spajanju vidjet ćete upit
za prihvaćanje host ključa. Prihvaćanje je očekivano i sigurno.

Tip / Savjet: "rsync -a <source>/ <destination>/" mirrors a directory tree
including permissions and ownership. scp and sftp both move files over SSH
— either is acceptable.
"rsync -a <izvor>/ <odredište>/" zrcali stablo direktorija uključujući
dozvole i vlasništvo. scp i sftp oboje prenose datoteke preko SSH-a — oboje
je prihvatljivo.


TASK 5 — NFS Client: Automount Your Shared Export  (20 pts, ~18 min)
NFS klijent: automatsko montiranje vašeg dijeljenog izvoza
--------------------------------------------------------------------
The repo server (172.16.16.121) now also serves each student a personal NFS
export for exchanging files with the instructor. Configure your system to
automatically mount your export on demand.
Repo poslužitelj (172.16.16.121) sada svakom studentu pruža osobni NFS
izvoz za razmjenu datoteka s nastavnikom. Konfigurirajte svoj sustav da
automatski montira vaš izvoz na zahtjev.

1. Install and enable the autofs service.  (2 pts)
   Instalirajte i omogućite uslugu autofs.

2. Configure an indirect automount map so that accessing
   {{ rh134_nfs_local_mount }} automatically mounts your export
   172.16.16.121:/exports/{{ rh134_nfs_export_dir }} with read-write,
   synchronous NFSv4 options.  (10 pts)
   Konfigurirajte indirektnu automount mapu tako da pristup
   {{ rh134_nfs_local_mount }} automatski montira vaš izvoz
   172.16.16.121:/exports/{{ rh134_nfs_export_dir }} s opcijama za
   čitanje-pisanje, sinkrono, NFSv4.

3. Trigger the automount (e.g. by listing the directory) and confirm you can
   read the file welcome.txt that's already there.  (3 pts)
   Pokrenite automount (npr. izlistavanjem direktorija) i potvrdite da
   možete pročitati datoteku welcome.txt koja se već nalazi tamo.

4. Create a new file inside your mounted export named
   {{ exam_variant }}-submitted.txt containing the text
   "submission from {{ exam_variant }}", proving the mount is writable.  (5 pts)
   Stvorite novu datoteku unutar svog montiranog izvoza pod nazivom
   {{ exam_variant }}-submitted.txt sa sadržajem
   "submission from {{ exam_variant }}", čime dokazujete da je montirani
   izvoz zapisiv.

Tip / Savjet: autofs uses two files working together — a master map that
says where to mount things, and an indirect map that says what to mount
and how. The wildcard "&" in an indirect map substitutes the requested key
into the source path.
autofs koristi dvije datoteke koje rade zajedno — glavnu mapu koja kaže
GDJE se nešto montira, i indirektnu mapu koja kaže ŠTO se montira i KAKO.
Zamjenski znak "&" u indirektnoj mapi zamjenjuje traženi ključ u izvornoj
putanji.


TASK 6 — Containers: Build, Run, and Persist a Custom Web Server  (15 pts, ~15 min)
Kontejneri: izgradnja, pokretanje i trajnost prilagođenog web poslužitelja
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The dev team needs a small custom web server container running and
accessible — and it must keep running after you log out (containers do not
survive your SSH session ending unless you make them persistent).
Razvojni tim treba mali prilagođeni web poslužitelj u kontejneru koji radi
i dostupan je — i mora nastaviti raditi nakon odjave (kontejneri ne
preživljavaju kraj SSH sesije osim ako ih ne učinite trajnima).

1. Create a Containerfile in /home/student/webapp/ that starts from the
   provided base image {{ rh134_base_image }} and writes the exact text
   "{{ rh134_podman_image_text }}" as the content of /var/www/html/index.html.  (4 pts)
   Stvorite Containerfile u /home/student/webapp/ koji počinje od zadane
   osnovne slike {{ rh134_base_image }} i upisuje točan tekst
   "{{ rh134_podman_image_text }}" kao sadržaj /var/www/html/index.html.

2. Build and tag the image as {{ exam_variant }}-web:1.0.  (2 pts)
   Izgradite i označite sliku kao {{ exam_variant }}-web:1.0.

3. Run the image as a detached container named {{ exam_variant }}-srv,
   mapping host port {{ rh134_podman_port }} to the container's port 8080.
   Confirm "curl localhost:{{ rh134_podman_port }}" returns the expected text.  (4 pts)
   Pokrenite sliku kao odvojeni (detached) kontejner pod nazivom
   {{ exam_variant }}-srv, mapirajući port {{ rh134_podman_port }} domaćina
   na port 8080 kontejnera. Potvrdite da
   "curl localhost:{{ rh134_podman_port }}" vraća očekivani tekst.

4. Make the container persist across logout and reboot using a generated
   systemd unit (podman generate systemd or Quadlet — either is acceptable),
   enabled for your user.  (5 pts)
   Učinite da kontejner preživi odjavu i ponovno pokretanje pomoću
   generirane systemd jedinice (podman generate systemd ili Quadlet — oboje
   je prihvatljivo), omogućene za vašeg korisnika.

Tip / Savjet: a container created with "podman run" disappears when your
session ends unless something tells systemd to manage it.
"podman generate systemd --new --files --name <container>" produces a unit
file you can install and enable.
Kontejner stvoren naredbom "podman run" nestaje kada vaša sesija završi,
osim ako nešto ne kaže systemdu da njime upravlja.
"podman generate systemd --new --files --name <kontejner>" proizvodi
datoteku jedinice koju možete instalirati i omogućiti.


